.TH HTTP_CHUNK 3
.SH NAME
http_chunk \- queue a chunk of the body
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_chunk(http* " h ", const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR http_chunk ()
queues n bytes as one chunk. It declares the body chunked if http_chunked(3) did not. When the request is out already the socket is asked for being writable, http_canwrite(3) then sends the chunk. An empty chunk is ignored, it would end the body.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure or after http_chunk_end(3).
.SH SEE ALSO
http_chunk_end(3), http_body_flush(3)
